      "hints": [
        "General term: $\\binom{7}{r}x^{7-r}\\left(-\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{7}{r}(-2)^r x^{7-2r}$.",
        "Set $7 - 2r = -3 \\implies r = 5$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{7}{5}(-2)^5 = 21(-32) = -672$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $\\left(x - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^7$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{7}{r}x^{7-r}\\left(-\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{7}{r}(-2)^r x^{7-2r}$$",
        "To find the coefficient of $\\frac{1}{x^3} = x^{-3}$, equate the exponent of $x$ to $-3$:\n$$7 - 2r = -3 \\implies 2r = 10 \\implies r = 5$$",
        "Evaluate the term for $r = 5$:\n$$\\binom{7}{5}(-2)^5 x^{7-10} = 21(-32)x^{-3} = -672x^{-3}$$\n$$\\text{Coefficient of } \\frac{1}{x^3} = -672$$"
      ],
